- Use only stdlib (math, json, hashlib, statistics).
- LS fit: x_i = ln(dr_i), y_i = ln(e_i). slope = Sxy/Sxx; intercept = ybar - slope*xbar. p_ls = -slope (since e decreases as h decreases: e = C h^p, p>0 → ln e = ln C + p ln h; slope = p > 0 actually. Let's be careful: x = ln h, y = ln e; y = ln C + p x; slope = p directly. As h decreases, e decreases; y decreases as x decreases → positive slope p. So p_ls = slope. In my earlier equation I wrote p = -slope wrongly; correct: p = slope in ln-ln space.
